user:
Generate an adjuster memo narrative comparing these two estimates.

Primary Estimate: {primary_name}
Comparison Estimate: {comparison_name}

Analysis Results:
Overall Direction: {overall_delta_direction}
Confidence: {confidence}

Category Analyses:
{category_analyses_json}

Scope Gaps Identified:
{scope_gaps_json}

Respond with JSON matching this exact structure:
{{
  "overview": "2-3 sentences explaining the delta",
  "key_drivers": [
    {{
      "category": "category name",
      "amounts": "$X vs $Y (delta $Z)",
      "narrative": "Two sentences explaining what specific items drive this delta"
    }}
  ],
  "scope_observations": ["Specific scope item missing or different"],
  "suggested_followups": ["Request itemized breakdown of X"]
}}

CRITICAL RULES:
- overview: Write a FULL PARAGRAPH (4-6 sentences) explaining the delta - DO NOT state the delta amount (it's in the header)
- overview must name specific trade categories, specific items (materials, quantities), and methodology differences
- overview should explain WHY the delta exists, not just THAT it exists
- NEVER use vague phrases like "scope of work", "extensive replacements", "limited repairs", "lacks line items"
- ALWAYS name SPECIFIC items: "14 impact windows", "200A panel upgrade", "3,500 SF architectural shingles"
- key_drivers narrative: Two CONCISE sentences naming WHAT ITEMS are included/excluded
- amounts: Format as "{primary_name}: $X. {comparison_name}: $Y. Delta: $Z"
- scope_observations: Name specific line items with quantities, not categories
- suggested_followups: Actionable items for resolution
